# Ship roadmap

When the workspace has a root `ROADMAP.md` and the user asks to ship, continue a ship, or runs `/ship`:

1. Take only the next unchecked item under `## Now`.
2. Implement it, run local checks (`verify-change`), commit on a feature branch, push that branch, and open a PR with `gh` when authenticated.
3. Check the item, move it to `## Done`, append new work under `## Later` (or `## Now` only if it blocks what just shipped).
4. For something a person can install or try, add one `## Later` share item when none exists; draft `SHARE.md` in the PR, do not post publicly.
5. Report the PR URL and stop. Do not start another `## Now` item in the same session. Do not spend this Cursor turn watching CI — the OpenCode PR babysit hook owns further CI/conflict fixes (or `@cursor` escalation).

Hobby constraint: prefer local free commands, do not add paid deps, do not spawn extra agents to keep going.

Hard stops (ask and stop): paid services, ads, new API keys, money-charging deploys, force-push or history rewrite, deleting foreign branches, secrets, and any post outside the repo. Notify-to-self via the configured Google Chat / Telegram hook is allowed (not public posting).

If `ROADMAP.md` is missing, ask before commit and push as usual.
